<h2>3.3 System-Level Requirements</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>System Component</th>
    <th>Specification / Constraint</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Target Platform</strong></td>
    <td>Cross-platform Modern Web Browsers (Google Chrome 110+, Mozilla Firefox 110+, Safari 16+, Microsoft Edge).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Client Environment</strong></td>
    <td>Any desktop, tablet, or smartphone device with an active JavaScript V8/JSC runtime engine and viewport width &gt;= 320px.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Cloud Backend</strong></td>
    <td>Google Cloud Platform (Cloud Run managed container, Cloud Firestore NoSQL Database, Firebase Identity Services).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Network Requirement</strong></td>
    <td>Standard HTTPS / WebSocket connectivity over TLS 1.3 with graceful offline cache recovery.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Latency Threshold</strong></td>
    <td>Sub-150ms client-side reactivity for all filtering, aggregation, and view-switching operations.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>3.4 Software-Level Requirements</h2>

<h3>3.4.1 Functional Requirements (FR)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>FR-1: User Authentication:</strong> The system shall authenticate users via Firebase Google Single Sign-On and maintain isolated session states bound to the authenticated `uid`.</li>
  <li><strong>FR-2: Inflow Management:</strong> The system shall record, edit, and delete income records with attributes for date, source, monetary value, recurring flag, and optional notes.</li>
  <li><strong>FR-3: Outflow Categorization:</strong> The system shall record expense records with standardized categorizations (Housing, Food, Utilities, Transport, Health, Entertainment, Education, etc.) and payment methods.</li>
  <li><strong>FR-4: Budget Definition &amp; Adherence:</strong> The system shall enable setting monthly budget caps per category, calculating real-time percentage consumption, and highlighting near-limit (&gt;90%) or exceeded status.</li>
  <li><strong>FR-5: Visual Dashboard Analytics:</strong> The system shall generate dynamic graphs including monthly cashflow bars, daily spending trajectory lines, and category distribution donut charts.</li>
  <li><strong>FR-6: Multi-Year Reporting Suite:</strong> The system shall support a Dedicated Yearly Mode with a 12-month performance matrix table, annual total inflow/outflow cards, and cumulative savings growth curves.</li>
  <li><strong>FR-7: Structured CSV Export Engine:</strong> The system shall generate and download RFC 4180-compliant CSV files for both monthly snapshots and comprehensive annual ledgers with a single click.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3.4.2 Non-Functional Requirements (NFR)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>NFR-1: Security &amp; Data Isolation (OWASP):</strong> Firestore security rules must strictly enforce owner-bound read/write policies (`request.auth.uid == userId`). Zero anonymous write privileges.</li>
  <li><strong>NFR-2: Formula Injection Prevention:</strong> All exportable fields must undergo strict sanitization and RFC 4180 escaping to neutralize CSV Formula Injection threats in client spreadsheet tools.</li>
  <li><strong>NFR-3: Performance &amp; Scalability:</strong> Memoized selector pipelines (`useMemo`) must prevent redundant recalculations on unrelated state updates, ensuring smooth 60 FPS transitions.</li>
  <li><strong>NFR-4: Responsive Ergonomics:</strong> The layout must seamlessly adapt across mobile (&lt;640px), tablet (640px–1023px), and desktop (&gt;=1024px) with dedicated full-height sliding navigation drawers and touch targets &gt;= 44px.</li>
  <li><strong>NFR-5: Accessibility:</strong> Contrast ratios must satisfy WCAG AA standards (minimum 4.5:1 for body text) across all warm neutral surfaces.</li>
</ul>

<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<!-- 4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION / MODULES DESCRIPTION                              -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>4. Problem Description / Modules Description</h1>

<p>
  Aura Money is architecturally structured into seven cohesive, decoupled modules that communicate via a centralized unidirectional data flow. Below is a comprehensive description of the work and functional scope involved in each module:
</p>

<h2>Module 1: Authentication &amp; User Profile Management</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Scope of Work:</strong> Manages user identification, session lifecycles, and security credentials.</li>
  <li><strong>Implementation Details:</strong> Implements Google Federated Single Sign-On using the Firebase Auth client SDK. Bypasses the hazards of storing or transmitting raw passwords in application memory.</li>
  <li><strong>State Handling:</strong> Uses the `onAuthStateChanged` reactive listener to hydrate user profile attributes (Display Name, Email, Profile Picture URL, Unique UID). If unauthenticated, access to financial sub-trees is securely gated.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Module 2: Income &amp; Inflow Management Engine</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Scope of Work:</strong> Handles recording, tracking, and aggregating all monetary inflows.</li>
  <li><strong>Implementation Details:</strong> Captures income source metadata (Salary, Consulting, Investments, Rental, Gifts), timestamped dates, and recurring status flags.</li>
  <li><strong>Reactive Ingestion:</strong> Stores documents in user-scoped Firestore subcollections (`/users/{uid}/incomes/{id}`). Employs real-time snapshot listeners to sync changes immediately across all browser tabs.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Module 3: Expense &amp; Outflow Categorization Engine</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Scope of Work:</strong> Provides a frictionless interface for logging expenditures with instant categorization.</li>
  <li><strong>Implementation Details:</strong> Integrates an extensive catalog of predefined expense domains paired with distinctive color tokens and Lucide iconography for rapid cognitive recognition.</li>
  <li><strong>Payment Metadata:</strong> Captures payment methods (UPI, Credit Card, Debit Card, Net Banking, Cash) and contextual user notes, establishing an audit trail for downstream spending retrospectives.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Module 4: Dynamic Budgeting &amp; Variance Monitoring Module</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Scope of Work:</strong> Establishes financial guardrails and computes real-time budget status metrics.</li>
  <li><strong>Implementation Details:</strong> Computes the exact monetary variance: `Remaining = Budget Limit - Total Spent in Category`. Calculates percentage utilization: `(Total Spent / Budget Limit) * 100`.</li>
  <li><strong>Visual Alert Thresholds:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="badge">Within Budget</span> &lt; 90% consumption: Soft emerald indicator.</li>
      <li><span class="badge">Near Limit</span> 90% to 99% consumption: Amber warning indicator prompting spending moderation.</li>
      <li><span class="badge">Over Budget</span> &gt;= 100% consumption: Crimson alert displaying exact deficit amounts.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Module 5: Interactive Executive Dashboard &amp; KPI Metrics</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Scope of Work:</strong> Consolidates high-level metrics onto a single responsive command canvas.</li>
  <li><strong>Implementation Details:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Executive KPI Ribbon:</strong> Real-time summary of Total Inflow, Total Outflow, Net Savings Buffer, and Savings Rate (%).</li>
      <li><strong>Month Navigation Controls:</strong> Interactive temporal switcher enabling seamless historical browsing and future forecasting across calendar months.</li>
      <li><strong>Recent Activity Feed:</strong> Chronological ledger of the latest transactions with instant inline editing and deletion capabilities.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Module 6: Advanced Monthly &amp; Annual Reporting Module</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Scope of Work:</strong> Deep-dive analytical reporting with dual temporal scope (Monthly vs. Yearly).</li>
  <li><strong>Implementation Details:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Monthly Analytics:</strong> Features daily spend trajectory lines compared against cumulative averages, category proportion donut charts, and itemized timeline feeds.</li>
      <li><strong>Yearly Analytics:</strong> Aggregates 12 calendar months into a unified annual performance matrix. Displays side-by-side Inflow vs. Outflow monthly bar charts, annual category allocation donuts, and a cumulative net savings growth curve illustrating annual wealth trajectory.</li>
      <li><strong>Year Selector:</strong> Cycle through active financial years with previous/next controls or a quick dropdown.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Module 7: CSV Data Extraction &amp; Export Subsystem</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Scope of Work:</strong> Client-side generation of standardized, spreadsheet-ready financial files.</li>
  <li><strong>Implementation Details:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>RFC 4180 Compliance:</strong> Implements defensive quote wrapping and escape algorithms (`escapeCell`) to neutralize CSV formula injection exploits.</li>
      <li><strong>Unicode / Currency Support:</strong> Encodes all output files with the UTF-8 Byte Order Mark (`\uFEFF`) to guarantee seamless rendering of currency symbols (₹, $, €) across Microsoft Excel, Apple Numbers, and Google Sheets.</li>
      <li><strong>Export Scopes:</strong>
        <ol>
          <li><em>Monthly Comprehensive Report:</em> Executive summary, category variance, daily trajectory, and itemized transaction tables.</li>
          <li><em>Annual Comprehensive Report:</em> Annual KPI summary, 12-month performance matrix, category annual totals, and chronological 365-day ledger.</li>
          <li><em>Targeted CSVs:</em> Daily spending trends only, Budget adherence only, 12-Month cashflow table only, or Category distributions only.</li>
        </ol>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<!-- 5. CONCLUSION AND FUTURE ROADMAP                                          -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>5. Conclusion &amp; Future Roadmap</h1>
<p>
  The First Review milestone of <strong>Aura Money</strong> successfully validates the technical feasibility, architectural robustness, and user utility of a modern cloud-synchronized personal finance system. By unifying real-time data persistence, reactive budget variance tracking, multi-scale visual analytics, and standardized CSV exports, the platform provides a complete financial command center.
</p>
<p>
  Subsequent project phases will focus on introducing automated recurring transaction triggers, multi-currency conversion APIs, and customizable target savings goals.
</p>

